.TH QUANUXCTL 1 "January 2026" "QuanuX" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
quanuxctl \- QuanuX Control CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quanuxctl
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBquanuxctl\fR utility is the primary administrative interface for the QuanuX ecosystem. It manages the lifecycle of **Extensions (QXP)**, handles secure credential storage via the OS Keyring, and controls the internal MCP (Model Context Protocol) server.
.P
It is designed to be usable by both human developers and autonomous agents.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-install-completion
Install shell completion (Bash/Zsh/Fish).
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Extension Management
.TP
.B ext list
List all registered extensions in \fI/extensions\fR. Shows status (Stopped, Running).
.TP
.B ext run \fI<name>\fR
Run a specific extension in the foreground (dev mode). Automatically injects secrets from the keyring into the process environment.
.TP
.B ext start \fI<name>\fR
Start an extension in the background (daemon mode). logs are written to \fIserver.log\fR or specific extension logs.
.TP
.B ext stop \fI<name>\fR
Stop a running extension background process.
.SS Security & Secrets
.TP
.B secrets set \fI<KEY> <VALUE>\fR
Securely store a secret in the OS Keyring (Keychain on macOS, Secret Service on Linux).
.TP
.B secrets get \fI<KEY>\fR
Retrieve and print a secret value (use with care).
.TP
.B secrets list
List all stored keys (values masked).
.TP
.B secrets delete \fI<KEY>\fR
Remove a secret.
.SS Administration & Toggles
.TP
.B enable \fI<feature>\fR
Enable advanced functionality toggles, such as overriding technical UI boundaries with Baroque performances. 
.I (e.g., quanuxctl enable jaques-mode)
.TP
.B disable \fI<feature>\fR
Revert advanced toggles back to standard Institutional Compliance structures.
.SS Agent Capabilities
.TP
.B mcp
Start the QuanuX MCP Server in stdio mode. This is the entry point for AI Agents (Cursor, Windsurf) to connect to the platform.
.TP
.B skills list
List available Agent Skills (specialized instruction sets).
.SS Legacy / Bridges
.TP
.B bridge
Manage legacy SignalR bridge processes.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QUANUX_HOME
Path to the QuanuX root (default: current directory or detected).
.SH EXAMPLES
.B 1. Configure Rithmic Credentials
.nf
$ quanuxctl secrets set QUANUX_RITHMIC_USER "my_user"
$ quanuxctl secrets set QUANUX_RITHMIC_PASS "s3cr3t"
.fi
.P
.B 2. Run the Rithmic Extension (Interactive)
.nf
$ quanuxctl ext run rithmic
.fi
.P
.B 3. Check Extension Status
.nf
$ quanuxctl ext list
.fi
.SH FILES
.I $HOME/Antigravity/QuanuX/.env
.RS
Global environment configuration (optional).
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR man (1),
.BR make (1)
